# Stackra file contract:
# Purpose: the ignore rules of this app member: everything `stackra gen` writes stays out of git,
#          the gitignored root shims included. The committed contract, stackra.manifest.json, sits
#          at the member root, outside .stackra/. Same rule set as the root .gitignore, repeated so
#          the member folder keeps it when copied elsewhere.
# Boundary: ignore rules only. EAS does not read this file: the generated repository-root
#           .easignore decides what an upload carries, and it keeps the shims and `.stackra/` below.
# Runtime: node
# Governing contract: Stackra ADR 0294 decision 10 (generated output is never authored), ADR 0295
#                     decision 5 (generated tool configs, their root shims and the root .easignore)

# everything gen writes: the runtime entry, the gen modules, the tool configs, the icons and splash
.stackra/*
# template only: the generated samples are committed so they can be read beside their source; a
# real project drops this line once `stackra gen` runs in it
!.stackra/**
# the root shims of the generated tool configs, for tools that read only the member root (Expo CLI
# and EAS read app.config.ts, Metro reads metro.config.js, EAS reads eas.json, Vitest reads
# vitest.config.ts); each re-exports or copies its .stackra/ file
/app.config.ts
/metro.config.js
/eas.json
/vitest.config.ts
# build output
dist/
# Expo CLI cache and the native projects `expo prebuild` writes
.expo/
ios/
android/
# Maestro screenshots, logs and reports (`testOutputDir`)
maestro-report/
